# p-field (M8): P's x typed (PointRows.tsx: P's readout's x is its value field). A click on x
# (330, 690; the input 308.78..352 x 678.5..702.5 at rest) opens it with "2.00" selected: --card at
# radius 6 in a 2 px --primary inset, padding 0 5 (the input 53.22 wide in its 54 px box, "f(" moving
# 10 px left), the typing tip hung 34 px under the head at the row's right; typed text replaces the
# selection; Enter applies 0.123 as P at 0.12 (its lattice), the track taking the focus with its ring
# (call 3 g); "1.2.3" is refused: the --destructive inset and text and the refusal's tip; Esc puts
# 0.12 back.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
click 330 690
wait 16
shot open
type "0.123"
wait 16
shot typed
key Enter
wait 16
shot applied
click 330 690
wait 16
type "1.2.3"
key Enter
wait 16
shot refused
key Escape
wait 16
shot escaped
